WEBVTT

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.560
I won't kill you.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.240
You'll go to the Public Safety
Department's Foreign Affairs Section.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.240
<i>A real... Magical Girl.</i>

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.080
<i>She's beautiful.</i>

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:46.010
<b>Daily Life and Comrades in Arms</b>

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.140
What are you doing?

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:58.000
You should be more careful,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:58.730
Asuka.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.840
How?

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.770
You had a spare key made
without telling me?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.170
The JSDF has special authority.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.200
That's clearly illegal!

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:12.420
You shouldn't have started
a big battle on Japanese soil.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.120
My magic disrupts people's perception.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.930
Nobody knows who I am.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.650
It's still a mess to clean up.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.380
Show some consideration.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:27.680
That guy you saw today was Kim Kanth.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.980
A terrorist with the East
Asia United Front.

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.370
I see.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.540
It looks like there's more
to this than meets the eye.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.610
A new organization
is involved somehow.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.960
I wanted us to take him,

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.920
but the Metropolitan Police
 got to him first.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.240
He'll be pronounced
 dead tomorrow, I imagine.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:46.750
I didn't kill him.

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.960
Dead men have no rights.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.910
They're going to get the information they
want from him no matter what it takes.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.580
They're gonna hush
the whole thing up, huh?

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.720
I guess the Japanese
police aren't useless.

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:06.130
You really are better off with us.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.180
Sure you won't change your mind?

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:11.440
Of course I am. I'll protect
myself and my friends,

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.640
but I'm not joining the 
Special Operations Group.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.060
I see.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:24.610
<i>It feels so strange.</i>

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:29.370
<i>The things I'm used to seeing
every day almost feel like a lie.</i>

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.240
<i>Huh?</i>

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:45.220
<i>Did the perception blocking not work on her?</i>

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.180
Good morning.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.600
<i>I guess I was worried for nothing.</i>

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.780
Morning.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:54.880
Um...

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:57.000
I heard you were
at Iidabashi yesterday?

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.590
Oh, yes.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.570
Are you okay?

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.350
Yeah.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.110
I wasn't really hurt.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:03.900
I see.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.570
Sayako!

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:15.750
<b>Rub Rub Rub</b>

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.620
I was so worried!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.010
There was nobody at your house,

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:11.360
and I only got your text this morning!

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.870
I was at the police station.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.780
The questioning ran long.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:15.750
I'm so sorry!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.850
You don't need to apologize.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.460
I'm glad you're safe.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:24.000
Yeah.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.700
Jeez...

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.090
I can't believe the police would
interrogate a pretty girl like you all night.

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:32.270
Nozo-chan...

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.890
But really, are you okay?

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:35.880
If you want,

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.190
I can talk to my dad.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.190
I'm okay, Nozo-chan.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.490
Thank you.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.880
What's this about your dad?

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.870
Nozo-chan's dad is a police officer.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.300
He works at the 
Metropolitan Police Department, I guess.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:52.520
I heard it was the National Police Agency.

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:54.210
Are they different?

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:55.660
They're pretty different.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:02.380
<b>National Police Agency State Sensitive Compartmented Information Facility (SCIF)</b>

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:09.680
You were pretty into that,

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.970
Makina-san.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.720
We don't know anything about this
organization that's backing Kim Kanth.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.800
We need to make him talk.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:17.920
Yes.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.590
And between you and me,

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:23.130
it's kind of personal.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.560
Personal?

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:30.330
I heard a friend of my daughter's
was almost killed at Iidabashi.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.620
Was she okay?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.860
Yeah.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:35.870
It was close, but Rapture saved her.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:38.830
Well, looks like we owe the 
Magical Girl one, then.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.950
My daughter was really scared.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:45.340
They should've kept
this shit out of Japan.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.420
She's in high school, right?

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.480
Yeah.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.620
She's a bundle of energy. And very cute.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:53.230
I guess she didn't get that from her dad.

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:55.390
What does that mean?

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.400
What do you tell your
daughter about your job?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:01.100
That it's boring desk work.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:02.350
I see.

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.320
But I told her that the boring
day-to-day stuff we do

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.810
is what helps the cops
on the street do their jobs.

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:12.530
The Counter International Terrorism
Division Sensitive Communications Annex.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.000
Our office doesn't even officially exist.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.340
Now,

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.420
I think it's time to get back to work.

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:23.880
The drugs should be kicking in by now.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.750
Comrade Kim Kanth was killed.

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:59.200
We need to take revenge.

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.670
Now, don't go getting any crazy ideas.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.840
I have the perfect way to take revenge.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.400
Here you go.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.050
A present from my queen.

00:08:13.650 --> 00:08:16.430
A slightly early Happy Halloween present!

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:34.130
Want some?

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:35.940
Umm...

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.340
Don't worry.

00:08:37.340 --> 00:08:39.110
We're friends, right?

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.600
Okay, I'll try a little.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:51.710
Sayako needs a lot of calories
to maintain that figure!

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.490
No!

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.580
I was questioned all day yesterday,

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:59.680
and I didn't get dinner, so...

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.000
It's good that you're hungry.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.140
It makes me feel better.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.740
Right?

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:08.110
We owe that Magical Girl a lot.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:13.320
That was probably one of
the Magical Five, right?

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:17.440
Magical Girl Rapture.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.160
The girl who saved the world.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.720
I don't know if she saved the world.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.750
There's still wars going on out there,

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.500
and there's still terrorism, too.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.200
It was the first time humanity fought
an enemy from another world!

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.710
And we won!

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.960
That's plenty!

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.090
I see.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:40.760
What do strong girls like
that do most of the time?

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.060
What do they think about?

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.550
They've got incredible power...

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.550
The power to fight
an army by themselves.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.530
I think they're just doing their best.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.640
Doing their best?

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.090
Great power changes people.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.400
It can make them slaves to their power.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.520
Someone who's a saint when they're
poor might change once they get rich.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:10.610
I think the Magical Girls
are still trying their hardest...

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:14.010
To make sure that their
power serves them,

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.540
not the other way around.

00:10:16.450 --> 00:10:20.260
So that they don't leave the world
where things are still sane behind.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:28.690
That's just the way I imagine it.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:31.140
Oh, crap.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.120
<b>Queen</b>

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:43.120
<b>Calling</b>

00:10:46.260 --> 00:10:48.280
<i>My queen!</i>

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.450
Is it going well?

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:51.030
<i>Of course.</i>

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:53.960
<i>But are you sure about this?</i>

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.330
<i>Helping those barbaric terrorists...</i>

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:58.540
It's fine.

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:04.000
We're very bad Magical Girls.

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:10.210
Hey, Asuka-san,

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:11.550
do you like swimming?

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:12.690
I don't exactly hate it.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:14.610
Oh, great!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:15.650
Right, Sayako?

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:21.220
Sayako?

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:22.910
What is it?

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:26.510
Swimming, I said.

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:28.620
You okay, Sayako?

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:30.290
Y-Yeah.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.710
It's nothing.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.970
Of course it's not nothing.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:35.130
Out with it.

00:11:38.470 --> 00:11:39.340
Umm...

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:49.020
Sayako! Sayako!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.690
Sayako! Sayako!

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.270
Inhale.

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:01.290
Yeah.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:02.620
Now exhale.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:04.180
Inhale.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.720
Should I call an ambulance?

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:11.970
No, it's okay.

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:13.830
It's passed.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.250
Um...

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.790
About what happened...

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.690
You okay?

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.760
You shouldn't try to force
yourself to remember.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.760
No, let me say it.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:29.360
I got to go home, right?

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:31.840
And I guess nothing happened.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:35.010
But a lot of people didn't
get to go home, right?

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:39.280
I couldn't do anything!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.650
All I could do was watch.

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.730
It's not your fault.

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.560
You're not a Magical Girl.

00:12:45.560 --> 00:12:47.420
You couldn't save them.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.590
No, that's not it.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:52.050
I didn't even think of saving them.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:54.000
Until now, I'd totally forgotten that.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.620
It's not your fault, Sayako.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.510
It's the police's job to fight criminals.

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.510
Maybe, but...

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:03.760
But I'm so weak.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.660
That's not true.

00:13:05.660 --> 00:13:06.460
Right?

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:10.030
You're right.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.680
You're not strong, Sayako.

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:19.440
But it's better to be cowardly than to
pretend to be strong when you're not.

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:23.550
A human being who can
recognize their own weakness...

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.160
is tough.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:31.310
I knew someone like that.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:32.580
She...

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.240
Sorry.

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.210
I'll see you guys later.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.770
Give it up.

00:13:44.770 --> 00:13:46.500
You won't change my mind
 by calling me all day.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:47.880
I'm never going back to the army.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:51.090
There's been a terrorist attack involving
a Disas Magic Biological Weapon.

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.560
What?

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:54.280
<i>It's a Halloween-class.</i>

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.290
<i>At Shinjuku 3rd Avenue.</i>

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:58.480
<i>The Special Operations Group
has already taken off from Narashino.</i>

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:01.260
We wiped them out!

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.850
What's that doing here?

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:07.060
I've heard that leftovers from the war
are being bought and sold on the black market.

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:09.100
This is the first time
we've seen one in Japan.

00:14:09.100 --> 00:14:11.540
<i>Can the Special Operations Group
 handle it on their own?</i>

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:14.620
We have a unit trained
for anti-magical lifeform combat.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.250
But we don't know if they can win,

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.840
and it'll take time either way.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.580
War Nurse is on her way now.

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:22.540
Kurumi?!

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:29.170
She needs someone
in front of her to stay safe.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:32.930
She's currently the only 
combat-ready Magical Girl within

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:33.830
<i>Japanese borders.</i>

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:36.360
Shit!

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:54.500
I want you to fight the 
Disas Monsters with me.

00:14:54.850 --> 00:14:56.960
I can't do it on my own.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:01.150
But I'm not any good at...

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:01.920
Please!

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:04.510
It's not just our lives.

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.380
Many lives are at risk!

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.960
P-Promise me one thing.

00:15:12.960 --> 00:15:13.840
What is it?

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:17.390
I'm not...

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.850
I don't think I'm that strong.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:24.510
So Asuka-san,

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:28.200
please protect me.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:43.760
Magical Girl Rapture Asuka!

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:47.040
<i>A Magic Biological Weapon?</i>

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.470
<i>Do they know what we went through?</i>

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:53.180
<i>Those evil, soulless monsters...</i>

00:15:53.380 --> 00:15:55.930
<i>Why would you bring those things back?</i>

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.410
<i>Kurumi!</i>

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:07.540
Bear! Bear! Bear!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.690
Bear!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:10.270
Bear?

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:23.750
Bear...

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.890
Magical Girl War Nurse Kurumi!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.810
Sacchuu!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.310
You'll be able to walk now.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.220
Get out of here!

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:48.240
Okay!

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:51.400
Bear!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.740
Bear!

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:07.420
Bear...

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.880
Bear?

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:17.540
<b>Bear!</b>

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:18.260
Yes!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:19.530
Kurumi!

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.140
Don't let your guard down, chu!

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.520
Bear!

00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:39.240
<i>This doesn't make sense.</i>

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.950
<i>It's stronger than the old
Halloween-classes I fought.</i>

00:18:17.980 --> 00:18:18.930
Asuka!

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:19.850
Sacchuu,

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:23.310
monitor the enemy's regeneration speed
 and biological activity.

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.570
Permission granted to establish
a link to my senses.

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.300
Roger, chu!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.190
This is no relic of the past.

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:34.340
It's been enhanced!

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.750
But it's still...

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:39.460
...no match for me!

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:49.230
<b>Bear!</b>

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.880
Asuka-san?

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.150
Um...

00:18:58.230 --> 00:18:59.410
It's been a while.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.800
I missed you.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.250
You get the data?

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.900
Sure did, gobu!

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:16.290
War Nurse and Rapture...

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:20.650
They're going to pay for ruining
the queen's present.

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:22.430
Oh, you there.

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:24.320
You need to get out of here.

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.600
This place is off-limits right now.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.810
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:45.180
Thanks for your
dedication to duty, officer.

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:51.970
Munchy, munchy, munchy, munchy...

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.600
Let me have a single bite, chu!

00:19:56.600 --> 00:19:58.600
I just want one bite, chu!

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.510
Did you get hurt in the fight?

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.100
I'm fine.

00:20:02.280 --> 00:20:04.090
I'm good at healing wounds

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:06.640
and at not getting hurt.

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:13.220
It was crazy to go up against
a Halloween-class alone.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:17.250
But there was nobody else who could.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:22.080
Iizuka-san won't tell me your phone number.

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:25.580
I asked him to keep it a secret.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.760
Why?

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.040
I didn't want to be involved with
 Magical Girl business anymore.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:34.440
I didn't want to fight anymore.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:41.710
You always did say you wanted to quit.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:48.940
But you're the one who
asked me to do this.

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:50.800
But...

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.070
You're a terrible person.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:57.330
Making me into a Magical Girl,

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:59.360
and then running away.

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:05.720
I don't know what to say,
except I'm really...

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:12.570
Keep your promise from now on, okay?

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:21.720
I'm not a strong person.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:29.600
Another terrorist attack?

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.680
That's crazy!

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:33.360
Is it true there was a Magical Girl there?

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.930
Are there any videos?

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:37.520
Is it safe to have videos
of Magical Girls?

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.150
They're a state secret!

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.170
If you recorded one, I bet the cops
would come for you.

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:43.590
And you'd never come back, I heard!

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:44.740
Seriously?

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:45.950
Oh no...

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:50.580
<i>It's true that Magical Girls'
identities are state secrets.</i>

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.440
<i>But you're not arrested
for taking videos.</i>

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:58.000
<i>Our perception blocking magic works
just as well through a camera lens.</i>

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:01.510
Okay, everybody, sit down!

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.770
This is sudden,

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:08.100
but we have another transfer
student to introduce to you!

00:22:12.610 --> 00:22:18.370
I'll be learning here at this school
with you all starting today.

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:20.480
My name is Mugen Kurumi.

00:22:21.510 --> 00:22:23.450
It's nice to meet you all.

00:23:57.410 --> 00:24:00.670
When Magical Girls go to school,
it's lots of fun!

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:03.690
Indoor pools, swimsuits,
and fanservice, chu!

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:06.850
But something wicked is stirring
on the other side of the sea!

00:24:07.140 --> 00:24:09.220
Next time: "A More Terrible War."

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.840
<b>A More Terrible War</b>

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:11.550
A terrible premonition is getting
closer to coming true, chu!
